# Build-context hygiene: everything here is either unnecessary for the
# build, or actively should not enter an image layer.
#
# The context is the repository root because processor/go.mod replaces the
# core module with ../, so both modules' sources are required. That makes
# excluding the rest deliberate work rather than a side effect.

# Version control. Large, and its contents have no business in a layer.
# Note this means `go build` cannot stamp VCS information inside the
# container; the image's provenance attestation records the commit instead.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Release artifacts built by scripts/release-build.sh — megabytes of
# binaries that would be copied into the build context for nothing.
dist/
bin/

# Local environment files. Never in an image.
.env
*.env

# Test and coverage output.
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Editor and OS metadata.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Agent/tooling configuration with no runtime role.
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/

# The Go workspace. Excluded deliberately, not incidentally: a workspace
# would make the container build resolve modules differently from how a
# consumer does, and it lists ./examples, which this context excludes — Go
# fails outright on a go.work naming a module that is not present. The
# build is workspace-free, matching the GOWORK=off verification CI runs.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Documentation is not needed to compile the Collector. Kept out of the
# context rather than out of the final image, because the final image
# copies only the binary anyway.
docs/
examples/
deployments/
